  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A Nightshelf colony of mythic standing, carved into interconnected caverns within the Berg's interior. ☽'scar Ramtatus~ was founded during the Great Thaw's expansion period, lost during the Orca Incursion, and has since been resettled under the Frozen Peace. Its tunnels extend deeper than any official chart reflects — a fact attributable to both deliberate policy and the nature of what lies below.
    
    Bioluminescent fungi mark the cavern walls in patterns that are partly natural and largely cultivated. Fire-braziers burn in the public galleries, though many bear soot-stains indicating prolonged disuse before relighting. The colony maintains trade relations with Dawn Naong, a crystal-vaulted exchange hub in the Still Pools, and with Nightfall Shelf, the larger Nightshelf settlement from which its founding population was drawn.
    
    ## Founding and Expansion
    
    Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss brought settlers from Nightfall Shelf and drove the colony's expansion deeper than any prior charting effort had reached. Twelve new shafts were mapped in forty days during the founding push. The thickest fire-core veins measured three flippers wide at the surface, with geothermal roots extending to depths the guild-masters had not previously documented. Alnae~ Oss ordered certain tunnels left deliberately unmapped — a decision whose consequences would compound.
    
    Fissure-Dealer ☽'Sanctteinvaus, a Nightshelf merchant, participated in carving the colony from raw ice during this period and rose to prominence through early trade contracts.
    
    ## The Marker and the Corruption Crisis
    
    Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, an adjacent structure at the colony's deepest point, was built to anchor the ☽'shadow Covens' Order's authority in the region. Residents call it "the Marker" and largely avoid discussing what occurred there. Beneath the Marker lies a shadow-forge vault serving as a repository for artifacts including the ☽'somunis' Mist~Record — a fire-core tome documenting pre-penguin history, guarded by successive generations of keepers within those walls.
    
    Fire-core output from the colony's deep veins dropped forty percent over two seasons. Miners working near the Marker ceased finding ore and instead encountered an unnatural cold — described in accounts as a breathless, aware stillness. Alnae~ Oss attributed the decline to vein depletion. The miners who carried frostburn scars on both flippers from the deep work attributed it to something else. Veil-render Mairae~ performed sanctification rites at the Marker to burn corruption back from its foundations. The deeper shafts were subsequently sealed on the authority of ☽'Lucatransiius Glow-bringer, an enforcer of Pactum∴ne who later died defending the colony.
    
    Ice-memory disruptions near the Glow-Fissure — a known corruption breach-point in the deep warrens — indicate new taint seeping through old fractures. The sealed shafts have not fully contained what lies beyond them.
    
    ## Loss and Recovery
    
    During the Orca Incursion, ☽'scar Ramtatus~ was lost. Its perimeter observation posts along the southern channels collapsed — a catastrophe severe enough to drive the neighboring Qingqe'frostlings to commission systematic study of orca blood-magic as a survival measure. The Grulkzul Omega Strike, a catastrophic blood-working developed during the Shattered-Spire Assault, is recorded as having manifested at the colony.
    
    The colony has since been resettled. Trade flows. The forges operate. Young penguins are born in the nurseries. But there is a quality to the recovery — a precision that borders on frantic, as if the colony is working to justify its own continuation.
    
    ## Institutional Significance
    
    The Mandatum∴ccord — the law encoding secrets as debts and debts as grounds for erasure — was formally proclaimed in a chamber within ☽'scar Ramtatus~. Representatives of the Wake-Singers, the Icebound Exchange, and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order gathered for the proclamation, with Fire Keepers stationed at the four vents. The colony also gave rise to the Fissure☽ Aurora technique, which fractures aurora-light into usable fire through forced opposition of crystal and flame within the ice.
    
    Noctisum~, a merchant implicated in contested artifact transfers and hidden negotiations during the council crisis, and Grandmother Deep, identified in interrogation records as an orca who obtained Aurora Stack genealogical materials, are both recorded as residents — an unusual pairing that the sources do not explain.
    
    ## The Inscription
    
    In the quieter tunnels, offerings accumulate at unmarked alcoves: unforged fire-cores, crystal shards in patterns matching no known Nightshelf notation. At the junction where three tunnels meet, carved so many times the ice has worn nearly transparent: *'still here, still burning.'* No one claims authorship. No one needs to.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771574448490_0", anchor: "Twelve new shafts were mapped in forty days", text: "Twelve in forty. Forty percent over two seasons. Three flippers wide. The entry is lousy with round numbers, and every one of them should make the reader's hackles rise. The deep-ice administrative records from the founding push — which I have read, in their entirety, in a vault no one else has visited since my second assistant was reassigned — document *nine* shafts completed and three abandoned due to structural collapse. The forty-day figure appears nowhere in the ice. It appears in Nightshelf guild commemoratives, which are propaganda, not cartography.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574448490_1", anchor: "Grandmother Deep, identified in interrogation records as an orca who obtained Aurora Stack genealogical materials, are both recorded as residents", text: "An orca. Recorded as a *resident*. Of a Nightshelf colony. The sources do not explain this because the sources are terrified of it. Grandmother Deep is a Wake-Singer theologian operating from the Corpse Current. Her presence in ☽'scar Ramtatus~ was not residency — it was access, granted by someone with authority to grant it, for purposes no surviving record makes explicit. That I wrote 'resident' here is the limit of what the commission's terms of reference allow me to state.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574448490_2", anchor: "☽'scar Ramtatus~ was lost", text: "'Lost.' The passive voice doing enormous work. The southern channel observation posts did not 'collapse' — they were undermined by pressure-rupture tactics consistent with orca retaliatory doctrine, deployed after penguin deep-mining breached into hunting current territory. The ice-memory at that depth is unambiguous. I am tired of writing around this.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574448490_3", anchor: "Fire-core output from the colony's deep veins dropped forty percent", text: "See note on round numbers above. The actual decline was staggered and non-uniform across veins. But 'forty percent' is what the guild-masters reported upward, because guild-masters report in numbers their superiors can repeat at council. The Rofundis∴rupt, referenced in current dynamics, was not the first vein collapse here. It was the third.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout, source_anchor: "fire-core output from the colony's deep veins dropped forty percent"
  annotation "note_1771574448490_4", anchor: "Representatives of the Wake-Singers, the Icebound Exchange, and the ☽'shadow Covens' Order gathered for the proclamation", text: "Wake-Singers at a Nightshelf legal proclamation. Sitting across from the Icebound Exchange. I found three sealed drafts of the Flipper Accord in administrative ice — renegotiated in secret before the public signing — and the overlap in signatories with the Mandatum∴ccord's witness list is not coincidental. Someone was building parallel legal architecture. The main text cannot carry that claim on the evidence I have. The margins can carry the suspicion.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574448490_5", anchor: "still here, still burning", text: "Unsigned. Recarved so many times the ice has gone transparent. This is not sentiment — it is stubbornness compressed into four words, which is the only form of courage I trust.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
